hadiths[89]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2810","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two sins whose punishment is hastened in this very world: (one) oppression and transgression, and (the other) disobedience to parents."""
"2811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to pray Witr before true dawn (subh sadiq) breaks."""
"2812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to do good deeds before six things appear: the rule of fools, an abundance of police (oppressive officials), the selling of judgements (bribery), treating blood (human life) lightly, the severing of family ties, and the rise of a new generation who will make the Qur'an into musical instruments; they will put forward one of them to sing (the Qur'an) to them, even if he is the least of them in understanding of the religion."""
"2813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to do good deeds before six things appear: the rising of the sun from the west, the smoke, the Beast of the Earth (Dabbat al-Ard), the Dajjal, the particular calamity that comes to one of you (that is, death), and the general calamity (that is, the establishment of the Hour)."""
"2814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to do good deeds before the coming of (terrible) trials like pieces of a dark night. (In the time of those trials) a man will be a believer in the morning and become a disbeliever by evening, and be a believer in the evening and become a disbeliever by morning; one of them will sell his religion for a small amount of the goods of this world."""
"2815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to offer the Maghrib prayer before the stars rise."""
"2816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For my Companions, simply being killed (that is, sacrificing their lives in the way of Allah) is sufficient (as an honour and martyrdom)."""
"2817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bravo, bravo! How heavy five things are in the Scale of deeds: saying 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah), saying 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), saying 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah), saying 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest), and a righteous child of a Muslim man who dies and he bears it patiently, hoping for reward."""
"2818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes up residence among the polytheists in their lands (settling there permanently), the guarantee of protection (of the Islamic state) is free of him."""
"2819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The righteousness of Hajj (or the sign of an accepted Hajj) is feeding people and speaking to them gently and pleasantly."""
"2820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the servant of Allah and His Messenger, to Heraclius, the great ruler of Rome. Peace be upon whoever follows guidance. To proceed: I invite you with the call of Islam. Accept Islam and you will be safe; Allah will give you your reward twice over. And if you turn away, then upon you will also be the sin of the Arisiyyin (that is, the peasants and subjects). And: 'O People of the Book! Come to a word that is equal between us and you: that we worship none but Allah, and associate nothing with Him, and that none of us takes others as lords besides Allah. Then if they turn away, say: Bear witness that we are Muslims.' [Surah Al Imran: 64]"""
"2821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is the document by which al-Adda' bin Khalid bin Hawdhah made a purchase from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He has bought from him (peace and blessings be upon him) a male or female slave, on condition that there is no disease, no defect and no hidden wickedness (or deception) in it. This is a (clean) sale of one Muslim to another Muslim."""
"2822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The glad tidings of this world (refers to) a righteous dream."""
"2823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give those who walk to the mosques in the darkness the glad tidings of the complete light they will receive on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give the people the glad tidings that whoever says 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah' (There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner), Paradise becomes obligatory for him."""
"2825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give this Ummah the glad tidings of eminence, (the ascendancy of) the religion, exaltation, help and dominance in the land. So whoever among them does the deeds of the Hereafter (good deeds) to obtain this world will have no share in the Hereafter."""
"2826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give Khadijah the glad tidings of a palace of hollow pearl in Paradise, in which there will be neither noise nor any fatigue or toil."""
"2827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Buthan (a valley of Madinah) lies upon one of the pools of Paradise."""
"2828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent to the people of al-Baqi' to pray (the prayer of seeking forgiveness) for them."""
"2829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I and the Hour have been sent together like these two fingers (in the closest of times)."""
"2830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent with Jawami' al-Kalim (that is, comprehensive words whose wording is brief and whose meanings are vast), and I have been helped with awe (struck into the enemy); and while I was asleep, the keys to the treasures of the earth were brought to me and placed in my hand."""
"2831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent with the sword shortly before the Hour, until Allah Almighty alone is worshipped, who has no partner. My provision has been placed beneath the shade of my spear, and humiliation and disgrace have been imposed upon whoever opposes my command. And whoever imitates a people is one of them."""
"2832","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent in the breezes of the Hour (that is, at a time very close to the Hour)."""
"2833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have only been sent to perfect good character."""
"2834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was sent through the best generations of the children of Adam, one generation after another (that is, my light kept passing through the best lineages), until I was raised in the generation in which I now am."""
"2835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be quick to break the fast and delay the pre-dawn meal (suhur) (that is, eat it late)."""
"2836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rather, it is Allah Almighty who lowers and raises (prices), and I hope to meet Allah Almighty in a state where none of you has any claim of wrongdoing (or any right) against me."""
"2837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Convey from me (to the people), even if it is a single verse; and narrate the accounts of the Children of Israel, there is no harm in that; and whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire of Hell."""
"2838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your ties of kinship moist (with the freshness of maintaining relations), even if it is only by greeting with salam."""
"2839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one and the same (in rank and ruling)."""
"2840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The edifice of Islam has been built upon five things: bearing witness that there is no god worthy of worship but Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, establishing the prayer, paying zakah, performing Hajj to the House of Allah, and fasting in Ramadan."""
"2841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing has been placed for my Ummah in their early mornings (in rising and working early)."""
"2842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Water is sprinkled on the urine of a nursing boy (and it becomes pure), and the urine of a nursing girl is washed (properly)."""
"2843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Alas for you, O son of Sumayyah (Ammar bin Yasir)! A rebellious group will kill you."""
"2844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A house in which there are no dates, its people are hungry."""
"2845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A house in which there are no dates is just like a house in which there is no food."""
"2846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst mount of a man (that is, the worst support for his speech) is to say, 'People claim so' (that is, to keep spreading hearsay without verification)."""
"2847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How bad it is for one of you to say, 'I have forgotten such-and-such a verse'; rather, he has in fact been made to forget it (so he should say that he was made to forget it)."""
"2848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between a man and polytheism (shirk) and disbelief (the only dividing line) is abandoning the prayer."""
"2849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The difference between disbelief and faith is abandoning the prayer."""
"2850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between every two calls (that is, the adhan and the iqamah) there is a prayer, for whoever wishes to offer it."""
"2851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between every two rak'ahs there is the tashahhud (sitting for the tashahhud)."""
"2852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour there will be the days of harj (that is, widespread killing and bloodshed)."""
"2853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour you will fight a people whose sandals are made of hair, and they are the people of Hell."""
"2854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour you will fight a people who wear sandals of hair, and you will (also) fight a people whose faces will be (broad and flat) like shields covered with layer upon layer of leather."""
"2855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour, trials will appear like the dark portions of a pitch-black night (terrifying and one after another)."""
"2856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour, the forms (of wrongdoers) will be transformed, there will be incidents of sinking into the earth, and there will be a rain (of stones from the sky)."""
"2857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was walking about in Paradise, suddenly a river was presented before me, on both banks of which were domes of hollow pearls. I asked: O Jibril, what is this? He replied: This is the (river of) Kawthar which Allah Almighty has granted you. Then the angel struck the soil of that river with his hand and brought out pure musk from it. Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (Sidrat al-Muntaha) was raised up before me, and I saw beside it a very great and tremendous light."""
"2858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was asleep, the treasures of the earth were brought to me, and two bracelets of gold were placed in my hands. They felt very heavy to me and caused me worry, so Allah Almighty revealed to me that I should blow on them. So I blew on them and they both flew away (disappeared). I interpreted them as the two liars (false claimants to prophethood) between whom I am: one the man of San'a (al-Aswad al-Ansi) and the other the man of Yamamah (Musaylimah the Liar)."""
"2859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was asleep, a cup of milk was suddenly brought to me. I drank from it (so fully) that I began to feel its quenching flowing out from my nails. Then I gave what I had left over to Umar bin al-Khattab."" (The Companions) said: O Messenger of Allah, how have you interpreted this dream? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(It means) knowledge."""
"2860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was asleep, I saw people being presented before me, wearing shirts; some of their shirts reached the chest and some reached lower than that. And Umar bin al-Khattab was presented before me, wearing such a (long) shirt that he was dragging it along the ground (as he walked)."" (The Companions) said: O Messenger of Allah, how have you interpreted this? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(It means) religion (its firmness)."""
"2861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was asleep, I saw in a dream that there were two bracelets of gold in my hands. Their matter caused me great worry. Then it was revealed to me in the dream itself that I should blow on them. So I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted this to mean that two liars (false claimants to prophethood) would emerge after me; one of them was al-Ansi and the other Musaylimah (the Liar)."""
"2862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was asleep, I saw myself in Paradise in a dream. There a woman was performing ablution beside a palace. I asked: Whose palace is this? The angels said: It belongs to Umar bin al-Khattab. At that moment I remembered your sense of honour (ghayrah), so I turned my back and went away."""
"2863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Once Ayyub (peace be upon him) was bathing naked when locusts of gold began to fall upon him, and Ayyub (peace be upon him) began gathering them into his garment. At this his Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, called out to him: O Ayyub, have I not made you free of need of what you see? He said: Certainly, by Your might! But I can never be free of need of Your blessing."""
"2864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man was in a barren wilderness when he heard a voice in a cloud saying: Water the garden of so-and-so. So that cloud moved aside and poured all its water onto a stony tract of land. There, one of the water channels took in all of that water. The man followed the water and saw a man standing in his garden, turning the flow of the water with his spade. He asked him: O servant of Allah, what is your name? He told him the very name that he had heard in the cloud. Then the owner of the garden asked him: O servant of Allah, why are you asking me my name? He replied: I heard a voice in the cloud whose water this is, saying: Water the garden of so-and-so, and it mentioned your name. So what do you do in this garden? The owner of the garden said: Since you have said this, then listen: I look at what this garden produces, then I give a third of it in charity, I and my family eat a third, and the remaining third I put back into this garden (as its cost)."""
"2865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was standing at a well, drawing water from it, when Abu Bakr and Umar came. Abu Bakr took the bucket and drew one or two bucketfuls, and there was some weakness in his drawing. May Allah forgive him. Then Ibn al-Khattab took the bucket from the hand of Abu Bakr, and in his hand it turned into a huge leather bucket. I did not see any mighty man among the people who could work as strongly as he did, until the people (having watered their animals) made them kneel down in their resting places."""
"2866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was lying down in the Hatim when suddenly someone (an angel) came to me and cut open from here to here (that is, from the throat to the lower abdomen), then he took out my heart. Then a golden basin full of faith was brought to me, my heart was washed with Zamzam water, then it was filled (with faith and wisdom) and put back in its place. Then a white mount smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey was brought to me, which was called al-Buraq; it would place its hoof at the farthest limit of its sight. I was mounted on it. Then Jibril set off with me until he reached the lowest heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! Then the gate was opened. When I entered, there was Adam (peace be upon him). Jibril said: This is your father Adam; greet him with salam. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting, then said: Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous son. Then Jibril ascended with me until he reached the second heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! Then the gate was opened. When I entered, there were Yahya and Isa (peace be upon them both), and they are maternal cousins. Jibril said: These are Yahya and Isa; greet them with salam. I greeted them, and both of them returned the greeting and said: Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous prophet. Then Jibril ascended with me to the third heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! Then the gate was opened. When I entered, there was Yusuf (peace be upon him). Jibril said: This is Yusuf; greet him with salam. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting and said: Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous prophet. Then he took me up to the fourth heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! Then the gate was opened. When I entered, there was Idris (peace be upon him). Jibril said: This is Idris; greet him with salam. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting, then said: Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous prophet. Then he ascended with me to the fifth heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! When I entered, there was Harun (peace be upon him). Jibril said: This is Harun; greet him with salam. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting, then said: Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous prophet. Then he took me to the sixth heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! When I entered, there was Musa (peace be upon him). Jibril said: This is Musa; greet him with salam. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting, then said: Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous prophet. When I began to move on, he began to weep. He was asked: Why are you weeping? He said: I weep because a young man who was sent after me, more of his Ummah will enter Paradise than of my Ummah. Then Jibril ascended with me to the seventh heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Jibril. It was asked: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). It was asked: Has he been summoned? He said: Yes. It was said: Welcome to him; how blessed is his coming! When I entered, there was Ibrahim (peace be upon him). Jibril said: This is your father Ibrahim; greet him with salam. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting, then said: Welcome to the righteous son and the righteous prophet. Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (Sidrat al-Muntaha) was raised up before me; its fruits were like the earthenware jars of Hajar and its leaves were like the ears of elephants. Jibril said: This is the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary. There were four rivers there, two hidden rivers and two visible rivers. I asked: O Jibril, what are these? He said: As for the hidden ones, they are two rivers of Paradise, and as for the visible ones, they are the Nile and the Euphrates. Then al-Bayt al-Ma'mur (the Frequented House) was brought up before me. I asked: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is al-Bayt al-Ma'mur; every day seventy thousand angels enter it, and once they leave it, their turn never comes again. Then a vessel of wine, a vessel of milk and a vessel of honey were brought to me. I took the milk. He said: This is the natural disposition (fitrah) upon which you and your Ummah stand. Then fifty prayers every day were made obligatory upon me. I returned and passed by Musa (peace be upon him). He asked: What have you been commanded? I said: I have been commanded fifty prayers every day. He said: Your Ummah is not able to bear fifty prayers every day, and by Allah, I have tested people before you and dealt with the Children of Israel with the utmost hardship, so go back to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your Ummah. So I went back, and Allah Almighty reduced ten prayers. I came back to Musa, and he said the same thing again. I went back again, and Allah Almighty reduced another ten prayers. I came back to Musa, and he said the same thing again. I went back again, and another ten were reduced. I came back to Musa, and he said the same thing again. I went back again, and another ten were reduced. Then I was commanded ten prayers every day. Musa said the same thing again. So I went back again, and I was commanded five prayers every day. I returned to Musa, and he asked: What have you been commanded? I said: I have been commanded five prayers every day. He said: Your Ummah is not able to bear even five prayers every day, and I have tested people before you and dealt with the Children of Israel with the utmost hardship, so go back to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your Ummah. I said: I have asked my Lord so many times that now I feel shy before Him; rather, I am now content and I submit. Then, when I moved on, a caller called out: I have enforced My obligation and I have lightened the burden on My servants."""
"2867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was asleep when suddenly a group appeared. When I recognised them, a man came out from between me and them and said: Come. I asked: Where? He said: To the Fire, by Allah! I asked: What is their matter? He said: They turned back on their heels after you. Then suddenly another group appeared. When I recognised them, a man came out from between me and them and said: Come. I asked: Where? He said: To the Fire. I asked: What is their matter? He said: They turned back on their heels after you. So I think that none of them will be saved except as few as the stray camels left to graze untended."""
"2868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was asleep and saw myself performing tawaf of the Ka'bah, when suddenly a man of wheat-brown complexion with straight hair appeared between two men, with water dripping from his head. I asked: Who is this? The people said: This is the son of Maryam (Isa, peace be upon him). Then I turned to look, and suddenly a red-complexioned, heavy-bodied, curly-haired man appeared, blind in one eye, as though his eye were a protruding grape. I asked: Who is this? The people said: This is the Dajjal; among people, the one who most resembles him is Ibn Qatan."""
"2869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was asleep and saw myself at a well on which there was a bucket. I drew from it as much water as Allah willed. Then Ibn Abi Quhafah (Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) took it and drew one or two bucketfuls of water, and there was some weakness in his drawing; may Allah forgive him that weakness. Then the bucket became large, and Ibn al-Khattab (Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) took hold of it. I did not see anyone among the people drawing water as Umar did, until the people (that is, the camels) drank their fill and settled down in their resting place."""
"2870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three men were walking along when rain overtook them, so they took shelter in a cave in a mountain. Then a boulder rolled down from the mountain onto the mouth of their cave and sealed it upon them. So they said to one another: Look to the righteous deeds that you have done for the sake of Allah, and supplicate by means of them; perhaps Allah will remove this (hardship) from you. So one of them said: O Allah, I had very elderly parents, I had my wife and I had little children, and I used to graze (the goats) for them. When I brought (the goats) back to them in the evening, I would milk them and begin with my parents, giving them to drink before my children. One day (the search for) trees took me far away and I could not come until evening had fallen, and I found that both of them had fallen asleep. I milked as usual and, taking the milk vessel, stood by their heads. I disliked waking them from their sleep, and I also disliked giving the children to drink before them, while the children were crying (from hunger) at my feet. This remained my state and theirs until dawn broke. (O Allah,) if You know that I did this only to seek Your pleasure, then make an opening for us through which we can see the sky. So Allah made some opening in it, and they saw the sky through it. The second said: O Allah, I had a cousin, the daughter of my paternal uncle, whom I loved as intensely as men can love women. I sought her for herself, but she refused unless I brought her a hundred dinars. I toiled until I had gathered a hundred dinars and brought them to her. Then, when I sat between her legs, she said: O servant of Allah, fear Allah and do not break the seal except by its right. So I got up and left her. (O Allah,) if You know that I did this only to seek Your pleasure, then make some opening for us from it. So Allah made some further opening for them. The third said: O Allah, I hired a labourer for one faraq (a measure) of rice. When he had finished his work, he said to me: Give me my due. I offered him his faraq, but he turned away from it (and left it). I kept on cultivating it until from it I had gathered cows and their herdsmen. Then he came to me and said: Fear Allah and do not wrong me in my due. I said: Go to those cows and their herdsmen and take them. He said: Fear Allah and do not mock me. I said: I am not mocking you; take these cows and their herdsmen. So he took them and went away. (O Allah,) if You know that I did this only to seek Your pleasure, then open up what remains as well. So Allah opened up the remaining part too."""
"2871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Once a man was riding a cow, and the cow turned to him and said: I was not created for this (riding); rather, I was created for tilling the land. I (that is, Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)) believe in this, and so do Abu Bakr and Umar. Likewise, a man was among his goats when a wolf attacked and seized a goat. The man chased it and rescued the goat from it. The wolf said to him: Today you have rescued it from me, but who will be its guardian on the day of the wild beasts (that is, in the era of trials), the day when there will be no shepherd for them other than me? I believe in this too, and so do Abu Bakr and Umar."""
"2872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man was walking, dragging his lower garment (on the ground) out of arrogance, when he was made to sink into the earth, and he will keep sinking down into the earth until the Day of Resurrection."""
"2873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man was walking along a road when he became extremely thirsty. He found a well, so he went down into it, drank water and came out. Suddenly he saw a dog panting from the intensity of thirst and licking the moist earth. The man said to himself: This dog has been struck by the same intensity of thirst as I was. So he went down into the well again, filled his leather sock with water, then held it in his mouth, climbed up and gave the dog water to drink. Allah Almighty appreciated this deed of his and forgave him. (Remember!) There is reward in doing good to every creature with a moist liver (that is, every living being)."""
"2874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man was walking along a road when he found a thorny branch on the road. He removed it from the road, and Allah Almighty appreciated this deed of his and forgave him."""
"2875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man was walking in his fine garment, pleased with himself and with the hair of his head combed, when suddenly Allah Almighty caused the earth to swallow him, and he will keep sinking down into the earth until the Day of Resurrection."""
"2876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dog was circling around a well, and thirst had almost killed it, when a prostitute from among the prostitutes of the Children of Israel saw it. She took off her leather sock, drew water with it and gave it to drink, and she was forgiven because of this (good) deed."""
"2877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The water of the sea is pure (and purifying), and its dead animals are lawful."""
"2878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The true miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings (salawat) upon me."""
"2879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopting a simple way of living is part of faith."""
"2880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Righteousness is good character, and sin is what wavers in your heart and you dislike that people should come to know of it."""
"2881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Righteousness is that with which your soul is at ease and in which your heart finds rest, and sin is that with which the soul is not at ease and in which the heart finds no tranquillity, even if those who give verdicts give you verdicts in its favour, however many they may be."""
"2882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing is in three things: in the congregation (that is, living together with the Muslims or eating together), in tharid (bread soaked in meat broth), and in the pre-dawn meal (suhur)."""
"2883","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing has been placed in the forelocks of horses (until the Day of Resurrection)."""
"2884","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing is with your elders (that is, those senior in knowledge and virtue and those advanced in age)."""
"2885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and burying it in the earth is a good deed."""
"2886","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is that it be buried in the earth."""
"2887","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Arabic word bid' denotes a number from three up to nine."""
"2888","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dying from a disease of the stomach and dying by drowning in water is martyrdom."""
"2889","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One cow suffices on behalf of seven people, and one camel suffices on behalf of seven people."""
"2890","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At the time of sacrifice (udhiyah), one cow may be slaughtered on behalf of seven persons and one camel on behalf of seven persons."""
"2891","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Al-Bayt al-Ma'mur is in the seventh heaven; every day seventy thousand angels enter it, and then they never return to it again until the Hour is established."""
"2892","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the buyer and the seller disagree in a sale, both of them should cancel the sale (transaction)."""
"2893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The buyer and the seller have the option (to cancel the transaction) as long as they have not separated from each other."""
"2894","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The buyer and the seller have the option (to cancel the sale) as long as they have not separated from each other, unless the transaction is made with a stipulated option, and it is not lawful for anyone to part from his counterpart out of fear that he may cancel the transaction."""
"2895","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The buyer and the seller have the option (to cancel the transaction) as long as they have not separated from each other, or one of them says to the other: Make your choice (whether to keep or cancel the sale)."""
"2896","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The buyer and the seller have the option (to cancel the deal) as long as they have not parted from one another. So if they both spoke the truth and made (the merits and defects of the item) clear, their transaction will be blessed; but if they concealed (a defect) and lied, the blessing of their transaction will be wiped out."""
"2897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Presenting witnesses and proof is the responsibility of the claimant (the one making the claim), and taking the oath is the responsibility of the defendant (the one against whom the claim is made)."""
"2898","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Produce a witness, or else the prescribed punishment (hadd, in the form of lashes) will be inflicted on your back."""
